# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OakTend NATIVE BUILD environment template (Capacitor iOS/Android only).
# Copy to `.env.native` and fill in when producing an actual native build;
# `.env.native` is gitignored, same as `.env.local`. NEVER commit real values.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS SEPARATE FROM .env.local.example: everything below gets
# read at NATIVE BUILD TIME (Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into
# the JS bundle Capacitor ships inside the app binary) or is a Capacitor CLI
# config the native shell itself reads - none of it belongs in a Vercel web
# deploy's environment, and mixing the two risks a native-only flag leaking
# into (or being missed from) the production website's env by accident.
#
# TWO INDEPENDENT GATES CONTROL WHETHER "CONTINUE WITH APPLE" RENDERS
# (src/lib/constants.ts APPLE_SIGN_IN_ENABLED + src/components/
# AppleSignInButton.tsx APPLE_SIGNIN_ENABLED). BOTH must be on for the button
# to show, on web AND on native (the component has no native-specific
# override of this gate):
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGN_IN=on   (src/lib/constants.ts)
#   2. NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGNIN=1     (AppleSignInButton.tsx)
# As of 2026-08-28 the OWNER DELIBERATELY TURNED THESE OFF on the live web
# deploy so a fresh account/onboarding flow could be exercised without hitting
# the Apple button - see the comment above APPLE_SIGN_IN_ENABLED in
# src/lib/constants.ts. THIS EXECUTE PASS DOES NOT FLIP THE LIVE VERCEL ENV.
# It only adds the vars here, for the SEPARATE native build pipeline, so a
# native build can turn Apple Sign-In on for App Store review (guideline 4.8
# requires it whenever Google Sign-In is offered) without touching the web
# site Landen is actively testing on. Set both to "on"/"1" here when a native
# build is produced for TestFlight/Play internal testing/App Store
# submission; leave the live Vercel env exactly as Landen last set it until
# he says otherwise.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGN_IN=on
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGNIN=1

# Sign in with Apple's Services ID (Apple Developer > Certificates,
# Identifiers & Profiles > Identifiers > Services IDs). Same Services ID
# already configured as the OAuth provider's Client ID in Supabase's Auth
# settings for the web flow - the native plugin
# (@capacitor-community/apple-sign-in, wired in src/components/
# AppleSignInButton.tsx's onClickNative()) needs the identical value. Keep in
# sync with APPLE_CLIENT_ID in .env.local.example (server-side revoke uses
# the same Services ID).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICES_ID=

# Overrides capacitor.config.ts's server.url for a non-production native
# build (e.g. pointed at a staging deploy or an ngrok tunnel to a local dev
# server for on-device testing). Leave unset for a build meant to load the
# live oaktend.com site.
# CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL=https://staging.oaktend.com

# RevenueCat's public SDK keys, same values as .env.local.example - listed
# here too because THIS is the file that is actually present when `npx cap
# sync` / an Xcode or Android Studio build runs, if the native build pipeline
# reads .env.native rather than .env.local. Keep whichever file the build
# script actually loads authoritative and the other one just documentation;
# do not let the two drift on the real key values.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_API_KEY=
